@2jumpsina/dsh-context-guard README · Why this plugin has to exist：**In one line**: a long session is not a technical failure, it is a **bill that grows every turn**. This plugin
exists to put that bill in front of you at the one moment you can still act on it — after a turn has ended and
before the next request goes out.

@2jumpsina/dsh-context-guard README · The problem is measurable：And one real session, from the very repository this plugin was built in: **584 calls, 274M tokens, ¥31.66 — of
which 98.6% was re-reading context and 0.17% was model output.** That is the failure shape being addressed here:
no crash, no error message, just an invoice.

@2jumpsina/dsh-context-guard README · Language：All user-visible copy is bilingual (Chinese + English): the banner, the handoff draft, host logs and
the badge/banner UI text. Default is `auto`, and the two halves resolve it **separately** — they do not
look at the same clues:

@2jumpsina/dsh-context-guard README · Host state route：```jsonc
{
  "plugin": "context-guard",
  "at": 1790000000000,
  "config": { /* the table above; handoverPath returns a relative/file name only, never an absolute path */ },

